WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.023 --> 00:00:03.023
♪ [music] ♪

00:00:05.717 --> 00:00:08.351
Give me one minute,
and I'll show you how Memorystore

00:00:08.352 --> 00:00:10.783
can help you build blazing fast apps.

00:00:11.017 --> 00:00:13.751
Memorystore is a fully managed
in-memory store

00:00:13.752 --> 00:00:15.551
for Redis and Memcached.

00:00:15.552 --> 00:00:18.784
It automates complex tasks
of provisioning, replication,

00:00:18.785 --> 00:00:20.018
failover, and patching,

00:00:20.019 --> 00:00:21.983
so you can spend more time coding.

00:00:22.383 --> 00:00:25.718
Memorystore comes in various sizes
to fit your budget

00:00:25.719 --> 00:00:28.918
and integrates seamlessly
with your apps within Google Cloud,

00:00:28.919 --> 00:00:33.117
including the operation suite,
making it easy to monitor your instances.

00:00:33.317 --> 00:00:36.118
For portability it comes
with an import-export feature,

00:00:36.119 --> 00:00:39.817
so you can migrate your Redis instances
without any code changes.

00:00:40.083 --> 00:00:42.917
Setting up a new Memorystore instance
is a snap!

00:00:43.117 --> 00:00:45.184
You can create one using Cloud Console

00:00:45.185 --> 00:00:48.250
by choosing the tier,
location, capacity, and version.

00:00:48.450 --> 00:00:51.883
Or use <i>gcloud</i> command line
or APIs in Cloud libraries.

00:00:52.317 --> 00:00:55.718
Once created, you can easily scale
your instances as needed

00:00:55.719 --> 00:00:58.883
with very minimal impact
on application availability.

00:00:59.217 --> 00:01:03.051
Standard high-availability instances
are replicated across zones,

00:01:03.052 --> 00:01:04.950
so you don't have to do it manually.

00:01:05.283 --> 00:01:08.351
Your data in Memorystore
is protected from the internet

00:01:08.352 --> 00:01:10.950
using VPC networks and private IPs,

00:01:11.117 --> 00:01:12.950
and also IAM integration.

00:01:13.250 --> 00:01:15.351
For all the reasons we just saw,

00:01:15.352 --> 00:01:18.218
Memorystore is a perfect choice
for not just caching

00:01:18.219 --> 00:01:20.517
but also session management, gaming,

00:01:20.518 --> 00:01:22.651
stream processing, and more.

00:01:22.652 --> 00:01:27.351
So next time you're looking to create
a blazing fast app and save cost,

00:01:27.352 --> 00:01:29.583
take a minute to look at Memorystore.

00:01:29.750 --> 00:01:33.538
To learn more, check out
<i>cloud.google.com/memorystore.</i>

00:01:33.538 --> 00:01:35.817
[whooshing]

